 ### NELF
-- **Definition:** A neural volumetric rendering framework modeling scene appearance using light transport vectors, enabling realistic relighting and view synthesis of human portraits from only five input images [S2].
-- **Steps:** A UNet-style CNN extracts per-view features. An MLP regresses volume density and transport vectors. Environment maps are estimated to disentangle lighting. Trained on synthetic data and adapted to real images via a domain adaptation module [S2].
